From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm: msm: dsi: return payload length after command DMA

After a successful DSI command DMA transfer, dsi_cmds2buf_tx() returns
the aligned controller packet size including its header. A six-byte
TC358764 generic write therefore returns twelve bytes. Clients checking
that the payload was completely transferred reject this as an invalid
length; the SM-T531 bridge stopped after its first configuration write.

Keep the existing DMA completion and short-transfer checks against the
controller packet length, but report msg->tx_len through the DSI host API.
Internal maximum-return-packet and read-command calls already check
payload lengths, and the bonded non-trigger host already returns tx_len.
No packet bytes, trigger, clocks or timeout behavior changes.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
index a9df0e255..15d28347c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -1584,7 +1584,8 @@ static int dsi_cmds2buf_tx(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host,
 		return -EIO;
 	}
 
-	return len;
+	/* The host API reports payload bytes, not the padded DMA packet. */
+	return msg->tx_len;
 }
 
 static void dsi_err_worker(struct work_struct *work)
